Mon Oct 26 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Rodrigo Brito

- Security: require sudo-policy-wheel-auth-self and remove the
  /etc/sudoers.d/10-installer written by Lyra installers up to 16.1 RC 2,
  whose global "Defaults !targetpw" let every account sudo to root with its
  own password. The file is removed only when unchanged and when the vendor
  sudoers is in use; otherwise a warning asks for review.
- Compare the file with cmp instead of command substitutions, so the
  scriptlet prints nothing to the zypper output.

